From 0b40896f2d1e2c17e5f7e53337c113ac89dd537f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWorlds <openworlds@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:44:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] Character encodings as the JDK's

Strings, readers and writers honour the encoding (they always used UTF-8
and threw on bad input): UTF-8, ISO-8859-1, US-ASCII, windows-1252 and the
UTF-16 forms by their JDK names and aliases, malformed input decoded as
U+FFFD and unmappable characters encoded as '?', as the JDK's defaults.
InputStreamReader decodes as it reads (it read the whole stream first);
OutputStreamWriter buffers until flush. String(byte[], int hibyte),
getBytes(int, int, byte[], int) and String.join.
